      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "> More generally, the API provides no way for users to determine whether a signature that fails to validate failed because it's actually a bad sig,,or becasue it violates the BIP66 rules.\n\nLet me add this: If you want to check whether a signature would have been valid before activation of BIP66, then I think you need to run the appropriate OpenSSL version. https://github.com/bitcoin-core/secp256k1/blob/master/contrib/lax_der_parsing.h#L44-L48 clearly says that `ecdsa_signature_parse_der_lax` isn't meant to mimick OpenSSL. It just accepts all the encoding violations that happen to be actually present on the pre-BIP66 chain.",
      "user": {
        "login": "real-or-random",
        "id": 1071625,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzE2MjU=",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1071625?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/real-or-random",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/real-or-random",
        "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/real-or-random/followers",
        "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/real-or-random/following%7B/other_user%7D",
        "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/real-or-random/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
        "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/real-or-random/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
